      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_623ceff1",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: meme_image; hasOverallIntent: Harmful; overall-intent-description: The image depicts two people in medical scrubs attending to a goat in a pastoral setting. The overlaid text reads \"is that guy fucking a goat\" and \"god dammit carl...he is,\" suggesting a humorous or absurd reaction to the scene. The meme's intent is to create comedic effect by juxtaposing the serious, clinical appearance of the individuals (wearing scrubs) with the mundane or humorous act of animal care. While the content is not overtly abusive, hateful, or propagandistic, it may be considered harmful due to its potential to trivialize or mock veterinary or animal care work, especially if the viewer interprets the text as crude or disrespectful. The meme relies on shock value and absurdity, which can be offensive to some audiences, particularly those who view animal care as a serious profession. The overall intent is to provoke laughter through the unexpected juxtaposition of text and image, but the crude language may contribute to a tone that is dismissive or disrespectful toward the subjects or the activity depicted.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_c81e17b4"
